            <div xml:id="d839">

                <pb facs="0842" n="838" sameAs="frus:frus1939v03/pg838"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51 Salt Funds/229: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Chargé in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Peck</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-06-07T16:00:00-04:00">June 7, 1939—4
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>99. Your 359, June 4, 10 a.m., in regard to Salt Administration.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>Department is not in position, in the absence of knowledge of the <pb
                            facs="0843" n="839" xml:id="pg839"/> contents of the memorandum of May
                        26 described in your telegram under reference, to decide whether the
                        curtailment of the authority of the foreign officials of the Salt
                        Administration is likely in fact to prejudice the position of obligations
                        held by American citizens upon the security of the salt revenues in such a
                        way as to give those holders a cause for legitimate complaint.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>If you feel that the action complained of by Lockhart does afford ground
                        for complaint on the part of American bondholders, the Department authorizes
                        you in your discretion to make appropriate informal representations to the
                        Chinese Government in regard to the matter.</item>
                </list>
                <p>Repeated to Peiping and Shanghai.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
